  "date": "2026-08-06T19:50:51Z",
  "subject": "fix: kind CNPG tolerations -- explicit default-toleration pair, not null",
  "body": "The previous fix (null instead of an empty list) looked right in an\ninteractive kubectl patch --type=json test -- that path prunes null\nfields server-side before validation -- but ArgoCD syncs via Server-Side\nApply (syncOptions: [ServerSideApply=true]), and SSA validates the\nliteral submitted manifest against the CRD's structural schema first:\nreproduced live via kubectl apply --server-side, a flat 400 rejection\n(\"spec.affinity.tolerations: ... must be of type array\"). ArgoCD's sync\nfor both CNPG Clusters therefore never actually applied, and the live\nobjects stayed at the ORIGINAL [] value -- which reproduced the original\ninfinite-recreate-loop bug (envs/prod/storage/values-kind.yaml's previous\ncommit has the full mechanism).\n\nFixed by setting placement.tolerations (and lakekeeper.catalog.tolerations)\nto the exact two tolerations Kubernetes itself auto-injects into every pod\n(node.kubernetes.io/{not-ready,unreachable}:NoExecute, tolerationSeconds:\n300) -- a real, non-empty, schema-valid array, so SSA accepts it, and it\nalready equals what CNPG's reconciler will see live, so the comparison\nthat caused the loop no longer has anything to disagree about. Verified\nlive: one instance restart to adopt the declared tolerations, then stable\n\"Cluster in healthy state\" for both mon-data and lakekeeper-db.\n\nhack/lint.sh's -skip Cluster workaround (added for the null attempt) is\nno longer needed -- reverted; the kind-values render validates Cluster\nobjects fully again.\n\nmake lint green.\n\n(per Task 4 in deliverables/plans/2026-08-06-datalake-v2-tenant-port-plan.md)\n"
}
